Linyaps Rust Debian packaging
=============================

The package is built with dh-rust against crate source packages from the
Debian Cargo registry.  Cargo is configured by dh-rust to remain offline;
network downloads during the package build are not supported.

The feature-level Build-Depends list is the union of the direct external
dependencies declared by the workspace crates and the two bundled crates.
It is kept in debian/control because apt must resolve build dependencies
before debian/rules can run.  dh-rust's X-Cargo-Crates mapping then assigns
the application crates to the two binary packages.

This upstream workspace contains private application crates and three bundled
crate sources: am-fs-erofs, the patched gix-transport implementation, and the
Linyaps workspace crates themselves.  Their licenses are recorded in
debian/copyright.  All other Rust dependencies must be supplied by Debian
librust-*-dev packages listed in debian/control.

The ll-init executable is intentionally rebuilt with crt-static after both the
normal build and the test phase.  It runs as PID 1 inside an application
container and must not depend on libraries from the host or container image.
